A SECOND, DIFFERENT KIND of `modules/<name>/NOTICE` file also exists, and must
not be confused with the four above: a **provenance note**, whose first line
says `<name> — provenance note`. Those are §2-style design-reference records
that live beside the module instead of in this file — the practice grew up
around the self-contained crypto/protocol modules, whose provenance runs to
hundreds of lines per module (`bls12_381` alone is over 800) and would drown
this file. They record what was consulted and argue why nothing is owed;
**none of them imposes any condition**, and `zig build check-catalog` enforces
that the two kinds stay distinguishable by that first line. Which kind a
module needs is decided by CONVENTIONS.md §5, not by module size.

So: to answer "does consuming zig-libs oblige me to anything beyond MIT?",
read the four files listed above and nothing else.

